# [Binary Digit Score](https://leetcode.com/problems/binary-digit-score/)

## Approach: Bit Manipulation

The idea is to count the number of set bits (`1`s) in the binary representation of both integers `a` and `b`.

### Algorithm
1. Create a helper function `find_binary(n)` to count the set bits in an integer.
2. Use `n & 1` to check whether the rightmost bit is set.
3. Right-shift `n` by one position using `n >>= 1` to process the next bit.
4. Calculate the set-bit counts of `a` and `b`.
5. If `s1 >= s2`, return their product; otherwise, return `s2 / s1`.

## Code (C++)

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int find_binary(int n) {
        int count = 0;

        while (n) {
            if (n & 1) count++;
            n >>= 1;
        }

        return count;
    }

    int calculateScore(int a, int b) {
        int s1 = find_binary(a);
        int s2 = find_binary(b);

        return s1 >= s2 ? (s1 * s2) : (s2 / s1);
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(\log a + \log b)\), since each helper call processes the binary digits of its input.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(1)\), as only a constant number of variables are used.

